  "is_prerecorded": false,
  "description": "Humans have honored midwinter since times immemorial, with feasts and festivals, rituals and magic - The festive season can be a time for connection and ecstasy as well as melancholy and isolation, and these moods inspire musicians from our region and around the world\n\nThis week on Convergence Zone, music for the solstice and inspired by the season -- from Michael Stearns, Tingstad and Rumbel, Erwilian, Clannad, David Arkenstone, Benoît Pioulard, Carbon in Prose, George Winston, Steve Roach, the Fischersund project, and more",
